* text=auto
*.db binary
*.png binary

# Vendored third-party bytes: NO line-ending conversion, ever.
#
# vendor/README.md publishes a SHA-384 for each of these so anyone can verify
# they are the bytes the CDN served. Under `text=auto` a Windows checkout
# rewrites sql-wasm.js with CRLF, its worktree hash stops matching the
# published one, and a verifier concludes the file was tampered with. The
# .wasm survives today only because git's binary heuristic finds NUL bytes
# early - which is a guess about content, not a rule, and not something an
# integrity claim should rest on.
vendor/** -text
vendor/sql-wasm.wasm binary
